  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_Final_Review_Q01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: What does 'Effective Access' show that reading the permission list
    does not?
  choices:
  - The date each permission was granted
  - What an account can actually do once every group and inherited entry is resolved
  - Which administrator set each permission
  - How much of the folder the account has used
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: A person can be in several groups, and entries can arrive from a parent
    folder. Effective Access is the only view that answers what they ended up with.
